VF43 and FIX144: two Louisiana passes, two failures, and the Alabama question answered\n\nTerminal holds at 203 of 346; FAIL_REPAIR_REQUIRED 56 -> 53.\n\n  al-trafficking-set              FAIL_REPAIR_REQUIRED -> VERIFY_PENDING\n  la-985-1-interim-expungement-set  -> BUILT_RASTER_PENDING\n  rcap-hi-custom-pleading           -> BUILT_RASTER_PENDING\n\nVF43 confirmed FIX142's two repairs on the bytes and improved on both\naccounts rather than repeating them. It found ELEVEN internal-vocabulary\ninstances on the pre-repair Louisiana canonical where the verifier named\nten, and it verified the Hawaii blank at the root: the pinned HCJDC 159(b)\nbinary's own caption reads \"Current Legal Name (Last, First, Middle):\", so\nthe delivered ink had told the Data Center the surname was \"Jordan\".\n\nIt also refuted FIX142's explanation of why the counters missed it.\nclassifyField returns the same {UNMATCHED, UNKNOWN} either way and no\ncounter compares a written value against a caption's format; the real cause\nis that captionAsksForEveryNamePart in rcap-field-semantics.mjs is\norder-blind. Un-stripping the label was a good change for a different reason.\n\nTWO FAILURES, NEITHER AGAINST THE REPAIR IT READ.\n\nla-976-arrest-no-conviction-set: FEE_AND_WAIVER passes, and eighteen further\ninstances of the same internal-vocabulary class remain on filed pages 1-8 of\nboth fixtures -- four on page 7 itself, the page that goes to a district\nattorney, including \"LegalEase completes only the participant-owned\nidentifying fields\". Its sibling was cleared to zero; the two now hold\ndifferent standards.\n\nnm_release_without_conviction-set: KNOWN_PREFILLS is clear and VF03's row\nshould be superseded -- all seven named fields read 0 at that base and 1 now.\nIt fails because delivered pages 15 and 20 print SIXTH JUDICIAL DISTRICT\nCOURT for Bernalillo (Second) and Sierra (Seventh) matters, and the wrong\ndistrict is SOURCE-SHIPPED: the master-library 4-222 binary prints it itself.\nThat is a source-acquisition obligation, not a build defect.\n\nAND A PATTERN WORTH THE NAME. WRAP_SAFETY is local to one script, but nine\nscripts share the same wrap-then-assert-the-same-width shape. Measured on the\nother five Louisiana families' delivered canonicals: la-976 12 of 23 pages\npast 552pt (worst 553.92pt, on a filed page), la-977 7/13, la-977d 10/19,\nla-978 9/14, la-985-redaction 6/17.\n\nFIX144 answered the Alabama identity question rather than handing it back.\nThe two packets are identical because both correctly refuse every election on\nCR-65 and they refuse DIFFERENT SECTIONS of it -- Section III is charged and\ndisjunctive, Section V is convicted, conjunctive and sworn -- so the routes\ncannot diverge in ink they must both refuse. It derived that mapping from\nwidget /Rect geometry because CR-65's field names are not in visual order.\nSix of Section V's eight limbs correspond to no collected input, which is\nintake and mapping; only boxes 10.6 and 11.0 are a genuine interpretation.\n\nIt also removed a retired eight-tick FAMILY_CONFIG entry sitting live at HEAD\nand ported the printed-elections disclosure to the pardoned family, where two\nconditional blanks had been listed flat under \"fill every one before filing\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W3FAJNotS5DdvyJS1khjid","timestamp":"2026-09-10T12:24:26Z","author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"}},"repository":{"id":1248656766,"node_id":"R_kgDOSmz9fg","name":"legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","full_name":"Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","private":false,"owner":{"login":"Roger-LegalEase","id":287531360,"node_id":"U_kgDOESNhYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287531360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase","html_url":"https://github.com/Roger-LegalEase","followers_url